# Copy to `.deploy.env` (repo root, gitignored) and fill in your target machine's SSH address.
# Used by deploy/deploy.sh (and the Rider Run Configuration described in DEPLOY.md §9.5) — the manual
# fallback path. The primary way to deploy is now the GitHub Actions workflows (DEPLOY.md §9.1-9.4).
#
# Use the restricted `ezbookdeploy` user and its forced-command SSH key (DEPLOY.md §1.4), the SAME key
# used by the GitHub Actions workflows — not a separate personal/root key. deploy.sh only ever sends
# the fixed commands `upload-release <ts>` / `deploy <sha> <ts>`, which is all that key accepts anyway
# (deploy/ssh-deploy-wrapper.sh on the server ignores anything else).
SSH_HOST=ezbookdeploy@CHANGE_ME

# You must also point ssh at the right private key, either via ~/.ssh/config for this host
# (recommended: `IdentityFile ~/.ssh/ezbook-deploy` in a `Host CHANGE_ME` block) or by exporting
# GIT_SSH_COMMAND / using an ssh-agent that already has it loaded — deploy.sh doesn't take an
# -i flag itself, it just calls `ssh "$SSH_HOST" ...`.

# There is no REMOTE_DIR to set anymore: the repo path on the server is fixed inside
# deploy/ssh-deploy-wrapper.sh (/opt/ezbook/app), not chosen by the client — this is intentional
# (DEPLOY.md §1.4): the forced command decides where things go, not whatever the caller asks for.
